    </aside>
    <div class="scrim" id="scrim"></div>

    <main class="main">
      <header class="mobile-bar">
        <button class="menu-btn" id="menuBtn" type="button" aria-label="Open menu" aria-controls="sidebar">☰</button>
        <a class="brand" href="#home" data-go="home"><span class="brand-name">RENOVO <span>GREEN</span></span></a>
        <span class="mobile-step" id="mobileStep">1 / 7</span>
      </header>

      <div class="content">
        <!-- HOME -->
        <section class="screen" id="home" aria-labelledby="h-home">
          <div class="hero">
            <div>
              <span class="kicker">Sustainable renovation planner</span>
              <h1 id="h-home">Renovate beautifully.<br><em>Live lightly.</em></h1>
              <p class="lede">Upload one photo of your room. RENOVO GREEN suggests a style, builds a costed list of low-impact materials and turns it into a weekend DIY plan.</p>
              <div class="hero-actions">
                <button class="btn btn-primary" data-go="upload">Start with a photo <span class="arrow">→</span></button>
                <button class="btn btn-ghost" id="heroSample">Try the sample room</button>
              </div>
              <div class="hero-proof"><span>No sign-up</span><span>Photo stays on your device</span><span>Progress saved automatically</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="hero-frame" id="heroArt"></div>
              <div class="float float-1"><span class="ico">📐</span><div><b>24 m²</b><small>room analysed</small></div></div>
              <div class="float float-2"><span class="ico">🌱</span><div><b>−38% carbon</b><small>vs. new materials</small></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="how">
            <article class="card"><div class="num">01</div><h3>Show us your space</h3><p>A single daylight photo is enough to read the room's light, surfaces and potential.</p></article>
            <article class="card"><div class="num">02</div><h3>Choose a direction</h3><p>Three styles matched to your room, each with a palette built from natural, low-VOC finishes.</p></article>
            <article class="card"><div class="num">03</div><h3>Plan, cost &amp; do it</h3><p>A live budget, a CO₂ estimate and a step-by-step guide you can tick off as you go.</p></article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- UPLOAD -->
        <section class="screen" id="upload" aria-labelledby="h-upload">
          <div class="page-head">
            <div><span class="kicker">Step 1 · Your space</span><h1 id="h-upload">Let's see your <em>room</em>.</h1><p class="lede">Drop a photo below. It never leaves your browser.</p></div>
          </div>

          <div class="upload-layout">
            <div>
              <input type="file" id="fileInput" accept="image/*" class="sr-only" tabindex="-1">
              <div class="dropzone" id="dropzone" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Upload a room photo">
                <div>
                  <div class="drop-icon">↑</div>
                  <h3>Drop your room photo here</h3>
                  <p>or click to browse your files</p>
                  <span class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Choose a photo</span>
                  <small>JPG, PNG or WEBP · up to 10 MB</small>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="preview hidden" id="preview">
                <img id="previewImg" alt="Your room">
                <div class="preview-bar"><span id="fileName">✓ Photo ready</span><button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="removePhoto" type="button">Replace photo</button></div>
              </div>

              <div class="card size-field">
                <label for="sizeInput">Approximate floor area <output id="sizeOut">24 m²</output></label>
                <input type="range" id="sizeInput" min="8" max="60" step="1" value="24">
                <p style="font-size:13px">Used to scale material quantities and costs.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <aside class="card tips">
              <span class="kicker">For best results</span>
              <h3>A good photo helps us see the possibilities.</h3>
              <ol>
                <li><div><strong>Use natural light</strong><span>Shoot during the day with lights off.</span></div></li>
                <li><div><strong>Show the whole room</strong><span>Stand in a corner and include floor, walls and windows.</span></div></li>
                <li><div><strong>Keep it sharp</strong><span>Hold steady and avoid very dark or blurry shots.</span></div></li>
              </ol>
              <button class="sample-btn" id="sampleBtn" type="button">
                <span class="thumb" id="sampleThumb"></span>
                <span><strong>No photo handy?</strong><small>Use our sample living room →</small></span>
              </button>
            </aside>
          </div>

          <div class="page-actions">
            <button class="btn btn-ghost" data-go="home">← Back</button>
            <button class="btn btn-primary" id="analyseBtn" disabled>Analyse my room <span class="arrow">→</span></button>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ANALYSIS -->
        <section class="screen" id="analysis" aria-labelledby="h-analysis">
          <div class="page-head">
            <div><span class="kicker">Step 2 · Room analysis</span><h1 id="h-analysis">A fresh look at <em>your space</em>.</h1><p class="lede">We read the light, surfaces and layout to find changes with the biggest impact and the smallest footprint.</p></div>
            <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" id="rerunBtn" type="button">↻ Run again</button>
          </div>

          <div class="analysis-layout">
            <div>
              <div class="scan" id="scan">
                <img id="scanImg" alt="Room being analysed">
                <div class="scan-grid"></div>
                <div class="scan-line"></div>
                <span class="tag" style="left:8%;top:14%">Wall surface</span>
                <span class="tag" style="right:10%;top:22%">Natural light</span>
                <span class="tag" style="left:18%;bottom:14%">Timber floor</span>
                <span class="tag" style="right:16%;bottom:30%">Soft furnishings</span>
              </div>
              <div class="facts">
                <div class="card"><small>Room type</small><strong>Living room</strong></div>
                <div class="card"><small>Floor area</small><strong><span data-bind="size">24</span> m²</strong></div>
                <div class="card"><small>Daylight</small><strong>Good</strong></div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div>
              <div class="card progress-card" id="progressCard">
                <div class="progress-top"><span class="kicker" style="margin:0" id="scanStatus">Analysing</span><strong id="scanPct">0%</strong></div>
                <div class="bar"><i id="scanBar"></i></div>
                <ul class="scan-steps" id="scanSteps">
                  <li>Detecting surfaces &amp; materials</li>
                  <li>Measuring light &amp; colour</li>
                  <li>Checking what can be kept</li>
                  <li>Matching low-impact upgrades</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="insights hidden" id="insights">
